{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great","id":1117883,"title":"[2e] Convince me Prime is great","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-18T12:28:43-07:00","id":1117883,"title":"[2e] Convince me Prime is great","content":"Now I haven't actually played the game yet, but when considering the types of characters I'd want to play someday, it always feels like Prime is a bit dull compared to other Arcana. Is that the case? I can see the appeal from a mechanical point of view, with dispellings and how it can interact with Hallows and Tass. But ... I'm having a difficult time seeing really cool stuff to do with it. With Forces you could control technology, command the elements. Life lets you heal and shapechange, Mind has a whole lot of broad stuff you can do with it. Etc. Prime, in contrast, seem a bit ... boring. Functional, but boring. <br /> <br /> So, what would you do with Prime in-game that makes it fun? In what kind of situations does Prime turn into something that's awesome and really cool to have many dots in, or lead to nice role-playing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11756-razikale","name":"Razikale","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T13:34:07-07:00","id":1117908,"title":"","content":"Admittedly, Prime doesn't seem like much at first glance; however, with a few more glances it does shine.<br /> <br /> Prime is the Swiss army knife of the Arcana; it has a lot of tools that you can use for just about any situation. Someone tosses a fireball at you? Universal counterspell. You need the key to this door? You can make a skeleton key out of nothing. You get into a fight with beings of Twilight, but can't quite hit them? Prime solves that issue just fine.<br /> <br /> Prime is also great in conjunction with other arcana. The more arcana you have then the prime arcana just gets better and better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T14:00:43-07:00","id":1117924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1117908#post1117908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime is also great in conjunction with other arcana. The more arcana you have then the prime arcana just gets better and better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Voltron...<br /> <br /> Also the Attainments are wonderful, specifically Imbue Item. I'll note that's also the level you get Apocalypse so the ability to record mage sight or imbued items that grant mage sight would be some of the most common items (everyone that can Imbue Items can make them, and the utility is obvious and ubiquitous).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-18-2017, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T15:39:51-07:00","id":1117963,"title":"","content":"God where do I even begin? I don't think I could make a character -without- Prime. It's like... well, yeah the swiss army knife of the Arcana is a good analogy. 2e Prime is a bit different from 1e Prime so I'm not as well versed in selling it as I was - but here we go.<br /> <br /> Prime is at the core of magic itself. By itself, it is probably not a very interesting concept because it seems like it is a religious tool more than anything else. In fact, the Arcana actually expresses that without other Arcana it is fairly empty. I personally kind of look at it like... coding? Most people using computers utilize graphical icons to run programs, not really understanding the code that goes into that - you might liken that to the use of Forces, Mind, Spirit, etc. Prime however would be the equivalent to understanding the very coding of the magic you are using. Utilizing that coding, you can use the powers that you have to do things that otherwise might seem impossible.<br /> <br /> One of the things I did in 1e with prime is I had a penchant for creating -worlds-. Fantastical worlds, impossible worlds that most people would say couldn't exist. My Silver Ladder would utilize Prime to create the illusion, and mind / space to solidify that illusion further. While illusions have been removed from the purview of prime, instead of creating solid 'truths', that doesn't change the possibility of that - the use of Platonic Form and Eidolon still seem pretty solid as tools to create and simulate environments and the like.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, Prime is not really a 'by itself' arcana. It's kind of a supplementary arcana. For instance, affecting resonance is all well and good - but your going to find a lot more use in altering resonance if you say focus on the spirit world.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T20:32:04-07:00","id":1118044,"title":"","content":"Prime's ability to mess with ley lines is basically a ready-made linker for Mysteries; whether you're observing what sort of phenomena are drawn to a node or pinning a bunch of lines together to try and give form to an Aetheric Verge, Prime gives you the tools to directly shake the tree of knowledge and see what falls out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T03:52:20-07:00","id":1118128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1117908#post1117908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly, Prime doesn't seem like much at first glance; however, with a few more glances it does shine.<br /> <br /> Prime is the Swiss army knife of the Arcana; it has a lot of tools that you can use for just about any situation. Someone tosses a fireball at you? Universal counterspell. You need the key to this door? You can make a skeleton key out of nothing. You get into a fight with beings of Twilight, but can't quite hit them? Prime solves that issue just fine.<br /> <br /> Prime is also great in conjunction with other arcana. The more arcana you have then the prime arcana just gets better and better.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ooh, what spell is it you would use to create a skeleton key out of nothing? Is it something like Platonic Form? But could you make one to fit a specific lock?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11756-razikale","name":"Razikale","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T06:36:47-07:00","id":1118149,"title":"","content":"It would be Platonic Form, not something like it. You can make Platonic Form take any simple shape, so yes it could fit in a specific lock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T06:47:08-07:00","id":1118152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Razikale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1118128#post1118128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ooh, what spell is it you would use to create a skeleton key out of nothing? Is it something like Platonic Form? But could you make one to fit a specific lock?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly Platonic Form for the first question. First the term skeleton key is use, let me also introduce a more modern term 'master key'. Both are as simple as a gemstone or sword. <a href=\"http://home.howstuffworks.com/home-improvement/household-safety/security/question710.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Master keys and skeleton keys don't open a &quot;specific lock&quot;, <b>they open <u>many types</u> of locks</b></a>. I'd say a good larceny or crafts roll, or the use of the encyclopedic knowledge or eidetic memory merits + having done research on master keys would be enough mundane help to know which type of master key to form the Platonic Form as, after that it's just a matter of making it. Basically it is the ability to turn something simple that is in your mind into a physical thing. VERY handy.<br /> Don't want to know the topic of locks and keys? Use magic to cheat and add Matter 1 Knowing. Prime can do it with knowledge or a little magic help to gain that knowledge. I would argue not knowing what you're doing will hamper any use of magic so requiring knowledge doesn't make it weaker.<br /> <br /> Also the Master Key/Skeleton Key locks within the same building tend to be the same type so you just made a key that will open most of the building with a single casting...<br /> <br /> Also from unarmed to carrying a sword is also handy and doesn't require any special knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-19-2017, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T09:55:52-07:00","id":1118199,"title":"","content":"Y'know when the big bad is basically Avade-Kedabra NPCs and cabalmates left and right with unmaking praxes and then you shut him down hard with counterspell after counterspell? That's an example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T11:51:06-07:00","id":1118230,"title":"","content":"The first archetype that pops into my head when i think of Prime is the anti-mage, someone whose magical specialization is disrupting magic. The ability to negate hostile spells is crucial to any warrior or assassin who targets enemy mages, but also to any guardian of magical spaces and any explorer of Atlantean ruins. It's also crucial for anyone who strives to uphold the Lex Magica, be they investigators, judges or executioners. Such individuals will also be greatly aided by Prime's ability to reveal and enforce Truth. As will diplomats and arbitrators, who also enjoy the protection from the rash or underhanded use of magic that abounds when tempers flare at the negotiation table.<br /> <br /> I think the issue is that while Prime can make for really cool and interesting characters, they will tend not to function very well outside the specific context of &quot;mage stuff&quot;. A magical PI or leyline stitcher isn't <i>useless</i> on a vampire hunt, but their utility drops off in a way you don't really see with the other Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T16:50:22-07:00","id":1118310,"title":"","content":"I personally find defining Prime's purview as &quot;truth&quot; first and &quot;magic&quot; later significantly help in making it more appealing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T17:19:02-07:00","id":1118318,"title":"","content":"What about a Prime Artificer. I do not mean the &quot;boring&quot; guy that just studies strong magical items (yeah, stuff created by archmasters, proto-portals to worlds unknown, cursed blades.... boring stuff :P ), but the mage that creates them.<br /> <br /> For example, here is a &quot;permanent&quot; self-recharging protective sanctum (with Prime 4)<br /> Mana Source: Find a remote (not contested) Hallow to use as a mana battery (with Prime 1 or create one with Prime 5)<br /> Mana Amplifier: Connect nearby ley lines to that hallow to use as Yantra and increase the Hallow's rating (more mana/day) (Prime 3)<br /> Security Capacitor: Imbue the area of the hallow with Celestial Fire and set the trigger to activate when something tries to cause harm to you/your cabal<br /> Mana Recharger: Imbue an other item within the hallow with Channel Mana to recharge nearby magic items (and itself) that are not at max mana using the hallow as source (Prime 3)<br /> <br /> Now, anyone that breaks into this sanctum and tries to harm you (or without the password) will get a baneful Celestial Fire to the face even if in twilight. The spells are triggered automatically by the imbued items and the imbued items are recharging automatically, provided the Hallow has enough mana.<br /> <br /> In my chronicle, the local Hierarch had a signature move to create Cleansed Patterned Platonic Javelins and throw them telekinetically (all in one turn as combined spell). Combined with his team and strategy (time/space wards), he surgically purged the local consilium of Seers in the past, gaining his current title of Hierarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","user":"Shadowjim12","date":". 07-19-2017, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T18:43:12-07:00","id":1118340,"title":"","content":"As Above so Below can turn basically any spell you can cast into a Praxis. It's easier to regenerate mana and WP for you than for other Mages.<br /> <br /> Prime is particularly good at turning you into a magical imposter, no one knows that you cast that trouble-making spell because it's Veiled to frame someone else.<br /> <br /> Invisible Runes basically gives you fast access to the Rune Yantra, you could even have it at Sensory Range.<br /> <br /> Wards and Signs, 'nuff said.<br /> <br /> Words of Truth can also double as a covert walky-talky system. The ability to communicate truth while speaking in tongues to your cabalmate who is waiting a half mile away for a report from your attempt at infiltration of a Pentecostal cult is not to be underestimated. Presumably it would work just as well if you were whispering or using sub-vocal communication. Heck, you could use sign language and the true words you're trying to send along would get passed to whoever you cast the spell on.<br /> <br /> Channel Mana, cast it on a Hallow, cast it on yourself, give it a decent Duration, say a month. For the next month you don't have to be anywhere near the Hallow to draw its daily mana from it. Become a Hallow prospector.<br /> <br /> Cleanse Pattern, whoops, there goes the mystical evidence that could have got you indicted at the Consilium or dogged by your political competition.<br /> <br /> Display of Power: This is how you get the Rotes that other Mages know so you can jot them down with Scribe Grimoire. Now you have a spell arsenal to rival anyone you probably know, even if you can't cast those spells yourself you can probably find a buyer.<br /> <br /> Geomancy: Any Node you need at a discount. Any Resonance you want as a bonus. It's been noted the subtle, but profound effects this will have on the Fallen and Shadow over time.<br /> <br /> Platonic Form: If you need a hammer, and are exploiting Channel Mana properly, then you will never run out of hammers.<br /> <br /> Stealing Fire: What are spell control limits? Seriously, create Sleepwalkers from your family or other Sleepers you're familiar with, you can probably bump them to Banner-Bearer with Reach, and then ask yourself if you really have to relinquish spells. Works great with Influence Mystery Cult or just Mystery Cult too. Bonus, they can't lie to you if they ever think they got the bum end of this deal because of Pierce Deception.<br /> <br /> Apocalypse: Is it really worth your time to investigate every Mystery personally? Wouldn't it be much easier to send out your Sleeper friends who have been bolstered with Stealing Fire?<br /> <br /> Create Truth: Fuck up your antagonist's carefully cultivated mystical landscape, and as a bonus distract them with entirely new Mysteries to Obsess over so they forget to come after you. If that doesn't work, just switch their Obsessions to one of your own anyway. Because as a Master of Prime you are a total Mage troll with <br /> <br /> Forge Purpose<br /> <br /> If you're trying to not turn all the Mages/Sleepwalkers/Sleepers in an area into your minions, then stick with Eidolon. Not as creative, but they can hold a fort down.<br /> <br /> Basically, my opinion of Prime is that it doesn't look that great on the surface. It looks better with other arcana, sure. If you really dig into what it can do on its own though you can find a -lot- of devious applications. Notice how I only drew from the published spells, then think on the fact that Creative Thaumaturgy is basically the beating heart of this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T20:10:48-07:00","id":1118384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1118340#post1118340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Above so Below can turn basically any spell you can cast into a Praxis. It's easier to regenerate mana and WP for you than for other Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Caveat that the probabilities aren't quite equivalent, but it's still another thing that can help you squeeze more out of spells you cast a lot with tools you use a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Invisible Runes basically gives you fast access to the Rune Yantra, you could even have it at Sensory Range. </div> </div> </div>I've asked about this and I don't think we've ever gotten confirmation one way or the other, but I suspect that &quot;short message in High Speech&quot; is not within spec for a spellcraft-booster that takes ten minutes to properly make at the height of Awakened power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Channel Mana, cast it on a Hallow, cast it on yourself, give it a decent Duration, say a month. For the next month you don't have to be anywhere near the Hallow to draw its daily mana from it. Become a Hallow prospector. </div> </div> </div>Channel Mana's touch-based.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Display of Power: This is how you get the Rotes that other Mages know so you can jot them down with Scribe Grimoire. Now you have a spell arsenal to rival anyone you probably know, even if you can't cast those spells yourself you can probably find a buyer. </div> </div> </div>Scribe Grimoire requires knowledge of the rote or access to a grimoire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T20:21:48-07:00","id":1118389,"title":"","content":"Man, imagine if we didn't had <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> to elucidate that mages are OP but not Broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T01:56:59-07:00","id":1118451,"title":"","content":"I have a Thyrsus mage in my group with Prime as her third Arcana, and so fare she has used it greatly in her investigation of a murder (discovering lying subjects, finding hidden rooms, unveiled compartments disguised as books, used it to hide the truth when she was lying, etc..)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T03:54:34-07:00","id":1118471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1118384#post1118384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've asked about this and I don't think we've ever gotten confirmation one way or the other, but I suspect that &quot;short message in High Speech&quot; is not within spec for a spellcraft-booster that takes ten minutes to properly make at the height of Awakened power.<br /> <br /> Channel Mana's touch-based.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that with the spell enhancing spells already a thing there isn't a reason that Invisible Runes can't be used to create what is one of the harder Yantras to get your hands on withough significant prep otherwise.<br /> <br /> Channel Mana: Creative Thaumaturgy could get around that problem creating a link between you and a source of Mana rather than turning a Mage into a Mana valve.<br /> <br /> Scribe Grimoire: Just cast it on your pal then so you can still build up an arsenal of Rotes.<br /> <br /> Oh, and add one to the list if we want to do CT, I don't see why you couldn't Perfect some Mana to use it more efficiently in Pattern Restoration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-20-2017, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T06:05:23-07:00","id":1118498,"title":"","content":"In the Channel Mana, is the touch thing just really fluff, like couldnt you get rid of that with a reach effect or just increase the distance factor. And if you couldn't, why would this spell be so completely different from all other?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T06:28:32-07:00","id":1118507,"title":"","content":"The default settings for a spell give it an area effect of about one arms length, centred on the caster. Presumably that's what Channel mana is doing.<br /> <br /> Adding extra factors should modify it just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T06:41:25-07:00","id":1118513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1118498#post1118498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Channel Mana, is the touch thing just really fluff, like couldnt you get rid of that with a reach effect or just increase the distance factor. And if you couldn't, why would this spell be so completely different from all other?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1118507#post1118507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The default settings for a spell give it an area effect of about one arms length, centred on the caster. Presumably that's what Channel mana is doing.<br /> <br /> Adding extra factors should modify it just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe explanation is that actually channeling the mana once the spell is cast still requires touching the subject of the spell. You can cast the spell through sensory range and it takes effect, but the effect itself is limited to touch (just like you can create a tool using Platonic Form at sensory range but not be able to use that tool until you actually pick it up). I think that limitation makes sense (otherwise you could cast the spell on touch range, walk away, and still be able to channel mana wherever you go) but I understand if people wish to ignore that limit or at least add a Reach that does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 07-20-2017, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T06:47:51-07:00","id":1118516,"title":"","content":"You could also use space and just co-locate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T06:57:29-07:00","id":1118519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1118516#post1118516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also use space and just co-locate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trying to show the benefit of Prime, not Space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T07:00:06-07:00","id":1118521,"title":"","content":"Well we did say it works best with other arcarna, didn't we?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T10:21:00-07:00","id":1118604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1118471#post1118471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that with the spell enhancing spells already a thing there isn't a reason that Invisible Runes can't be used to create what is one of the harder Yantras to get your hands on withough significant prep otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a two-dot spell and the nature of other Yantras suggests that Runes give a higher bonus than +1 despite their versatility specifically because they can be seen and disrupted; you wouldn't let High Speech apply its bonus without talking, so why on earth would you let Runes apply with <i>invisible and erasure-resistant writing that can be done instantaneously</i>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Scribe Grimoire: Just cast it on your pal then so you can still build up an arsenal of Rotes. </div> </div> </div>Your pal is not a grimoire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T10:59:52-07:00","id":1118620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1118604#post1118604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a two-dot spell and the nature of other Yantras suggests that Runes give a higher bonus than +1 despite their versatility specifically because they can be seen and disrupted; you wouldn't let High Speech apply its bonus without talking, so why on earth would you let Runes apply with <i>invisible and erasure-resistant writing that can be done instantaneously</i>?<br /> <br /> Your pal is not a grimoire.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're going to just have to agree to disagree.<br /> <br /> The pal probably knows spells you don't and if he has Scribe Grimoire cast on him he can copy them down even if he doesn't have Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T11:26:28-07:00","id":1118636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1118620#post1118620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're going to just have to agree to disagree.<br /> <br /> The pal probably knows spells you don't and if he has Scribe Grimoire cast on him he can copy them down even if he doesn't have Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scribe Grimoire isn't a spell you cast on yourself that lets you write down rotes, it's a spell that writes down rotes. That's like casting Thunderbolt on someone to give them the ability to throw thunderbolts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T11:38:19-07:00","id":1118640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1118636#post1118636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scribe Grimoire isn't a spell you cast on yourself that lets you write down rotes, it's a spell that writes down rotes. That's like casting Thunderbolt on someone to give them the ability to throw thunderbolts.</div> </div> </div> </div>On another note. That would be a cool spell. Are we sure we can't figure that out? Maybe create a spell that lets you catch a spell cast on you to recast later. Maybe that's for the Thaumaturgy thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13691-margul","name":"Margul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T12:02:02-07:00","id":1118648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Margul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1118640#post1118640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note. That would be a cool spell. Are we sure we can't figure that out? Maybe create a spell that lets you catch a spell cast on you to recast later. Maybe that's for the Thaumaturgy thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imbue Item. You could craft a wand of <i>Scribe Grimoire.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 07-20-2017, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T12:05:22-07:00","id":1118650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Margul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1118640#post1118640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note. That would be a cool spell. Are we sure we can't figure that out? Maybe create a spell that lets you catch a spell cast on you to recast later. Maybe that's for the Thaumaturgy thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do a crude version of &quot;here, have a Thunderbolt&quot; by using Hung Spell with a Conditional Duration the target can trigger. Well, not Thunderbolt I guess, because I think hung spells have a pre-determined target, but you can give someone a one-time use of Shapeshifting for example.<br /> <br /> Catching a spell sounds cool as heck, and is almost definitely a Prime + Time spell.<br /> <br /> Hmm. Is altering a forming imago within the purview of Prime? I'm pretty sure no non-Archmaster magic can alter a spell that's already been cast, only suppress, but could someone with sufficient knowledge of Prime (and probably the Arcanum being used) alter a spell <i>as</i> it is bing cast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T12:57:24-07:00","id":1118671,"title":"","content":"I think it would be awesome. You could give a spell to an ally and they could cast it whenever they needed. I think you're right about the arcanum. It would be similar to the hang spell attainment or maybe counterspell. I decided to ask the people on the thaumaturgy thread to help out and actually make the spell. We might be able to alter a forming imago with mind maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13691-margul","name":"Margul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T13:25:25-07:00","id":1118682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1118648#post1118648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imbue Item. You could craft a wand of <i>Scribe Grimoire.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>You mean that Fountain Pen of <i>Scribe Grimoire</i> or bluetooth keyboard of <i>Scribe Grimoire</i>? That's great!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T15:30:42-07:00","id":1118724,"title":"","content":"If you want to take precedent from 1e it's entirely possible to give an entity the use of a spell to be triggered at their leisure for their benefit. It wouldn't be out of bounds to have Scribe Grimoire function in a similar fashion, or any other spell really. I know there was a bit in the previews of SoS about imbuing living beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T17:06:57-07:00","id":1118764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Margul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1118671#post1118671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be awesome. You could give a spell to an ally and they could cast it whenever they needed. I think you're right about the arcanum. It would be similar to the hang spell attainment or maybe counterspell. I decided to ask the people on the thaumaturgy thread to help out and actually make the spell. We might be able to alter a forming imago with mind maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Point of order: Hung Spell is a spell, not an Attainment. It's often used in conjunction with the Conditional Duration Attainment to give it a trigger other than &quot;the mage feels like it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also I'm not 100% sure this is explicitly stated in 2e, but last I heard an imago is explicitly immune to Mind magic. It's a construction of the soul, not of the mind.<br /> <br /> And while I'm pretty sure it's okay to &quot;freeze&quot; a spell (perhaps for later study) using Prime + Time, I'm not sure if throwing it back in the caster's face is permissible. See, the target of a spell is part of its imago, and under normal circumstances it is impossible to alter - you can selectively suppress or cancel parts of a spell (either automatically if it's your spell or forcibly through Dispel Magic) but you can't <i>change</i> it. Altering a spell like that is arguably a Prime Weaving (or even Ruling) effect, but I suspect this might be one of those things like soul creation you're not supposed to be able to mess with, at least not short of archmastery. I'm not sure, though, so I'd love to hear everyone else's opinions. At the very least, though, redirecting the spell would require an additional, separate spell on top of the one that &quot;captured&quot; it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T02:12:49-07:00","id":1118869,"title":"","content":"People like to say that the imago is something mystical and untouchable, but the intro text to the Life Arcanum mentions that Life can be used to change the neurons in the brain that is used for forming imagos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T04:10:29-07:00","id":1118898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1118869#post1118869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People like to say that the imago is something mystical and untouchable, but the intro text to the Life Arcanum mentions that Life can be used to change the neurons in the brain that is used for forming imagos.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding of that is that it's possible to use Mind or Life to change the behavior of a mage to make them choose to cast (or not cast) in the way that you want, but you can't interfere directly with their casting. Kind of like how Mind can make someone to throw a ball, but can't directly influence the force and trajectory of the throw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T05:38:04-07:00","id":1118922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1117883-2e-convince-me-prime-is-great?p=1118869#post1118869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People like to say that the imago is something mystical and untouchable, but the intro text to the Life Arcanum mentions that Life can be used to change the neurons in the brain that is used for forming imagos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see that part as emphasizing Life's ability to affect the ability for cognition and abstract thinking, which are the basis for Imagos. A much needed emphasis, because the game doesn't want us to think that affecting the cerebral is solely Mind's domain.<br /> <br /> Affecting the particulars of Gnostic channeling that use one's mental capacity as a medium is... probably not what the writers were intending, given that Imagos are indeed mystical. Not untouchable, but still mystical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T13:44:00-07:00","id":1120054,"title":"","content":"Having read 2e. It's internally consistent but not very balanced in my opinion. Unless you have prime, two masters fighting each other will most likely kill one another in one strike. I know what dave was going for but in practice it's not fun. My point is, prime is the most necessary arcana to deal with enemy mages. Prime shield can't get ignored with exceptional successes like threshold and it can counter magic. All in all can't say I'm a fan of 2e's gameplay but prime is probably the most useful arcana. It's the metamagic ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}